### AixBOMS data stack, Phase 1: example requests
### Open in VS Code with the "REST Client" extension (or IntelliJ) and click "Send Request".
### Run them top to bottom: later requests reuse ids from earlier responses.

@api = http://localhost:8080/api

### 1. The rack list the UI shows: racks + children + administrators (a GraphQL view served as REST)
GET {{api}}/views/rack-overview?page=0&size=20

### 2. Same view, filtered by name (SQL LIKE pattern, % encoded as %25)
GET {{api}}/views/rack-overview?name=LYO%25

### 3. Create a person (a human)
# @name person
POST {{api}}/persons
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Lea Bernard", "personType": "HUMAN",
  "contact": { "email": "lea.bernard@example.com", "phone": "+33 6 00 00 00 00" } }

### 4. Create a person (an AI agent: different contact fields, same JSON attribute)
# @name agent
POST {{api}}/persons
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Capacity Agent", "personType": "AI",
  "contact": { "endpoint": "https://agents.example.com/capacity" } }

### 5. Create a rack
# @name rack
POST {{api}}/racks
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "STE-R02", "serialNumber": "RK-0300", "heightUnits": 42 }

### 6. Create a server inside that rack
# @name server
POST {{api}}/components
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "srv-web-01", "serialNumber": "SN-12001", "rackId": "{{rack.response.body.id}}" }

### 7. Make Lea primary administrator
POST {{api}}/racks/{{rack.response.body.id}}/administrators
Content-Type: application/json

{ "personId": "{{person.response.body.id}}", "primaryAdministrator": true }

### 8. Make the agent primary too: rule SinglePrimaryAdministrator demotes Lea
POST {{api}}/racks/{{rack.response.body.id}}/administrators
Content-Type: application/json

{ "personId": "{{agent.response.body.id}}", "primaryAdministrator": true }

### 9. Check: the agent is primary, Lea is not
GET {{api}}/racks/{{rack.response.body.id}}/administrators

### 10. Give Lea the primary role back
PATCH {{api}}/racks/{{rack.response.body.id}}/administrators/{{person.response.body.id}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "primaryAdministrator": true }

### 11. Remove the agent as administrator
DELETE {{api}}/racks/{{rack.response.body.id}}/administrators/{{agent.response.body.id}}

### 12. Try to delete the rack while the server is still in it -> 409 dcim.rackNotEmpty
DELETE {{api}}/racks/{{rack.response.body.id}}

### 13. Take the server out of the rack (the server is kept)
DELETE {{api}}/racks/{{rack.response.body.id}}/children/{{server.response.body.id}}

### 14. Put it back
PUT {{api}}/racks/{{rack.response.body.id}}/children/{{server.response.body.id}}

### 15. Update a person; "version" turns on optimistic locking (send the version you read)
PATCH {{api}}/persons/{{person.response.body.id}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "version": 0, "name": "Léa Bernard" }

### 16. Plain lists
GET {{api}}/persons?page=0&size=20

###
GET {{api}}/components?page=0&size=20

###
GET {{api}}/racks?name=STE%25

### 17. GraphQL directly (the same schema the views use). Browser UI: http://localhost:8080/graphiql
POST http://localhost:8080/graphql
Content-Type: application/json

{ "query": "{ rackCount racks(size: 5) { name children { name } administrators { primaryAdministrator person { name personType } } } }" }
